Subject: drawbench --gpu: what a frame gives the GPU to do, from the fake's counters

Per scene, for the last measured frame: the words the fake's command processor
fetched (and those inside draw-state groups), the registers it wrote, its
CP_LOAD_STATE6 packets and waits for idle, the draws it ran and those a tile's
visibility stream skipped, the groups run, the passes, tiles and binned draws,
and the megabytes the tiles' loads and stores moved (FakeGpu::Stats gains
loadedPixels beside storedPixels). --gmem-off BITS and --gmem-draws N pass the
plug-in's metal_gmem_off and metal_gmem_draws, so the same scene can be read
with a switch off (6080: the pass as it was before the draw-state groups) or
with every pass tiled.

Two scenes of a light frame, where the pass is seven layers the size of the
screen: V (one attachment, fixed blending: sysmem with the default bar) and W
(the second attachment bound, three of the draws reading their target: tiles).
The golden files gain their two lines; no other line changes.


